Hi Kevin,

Following up on the 04/03/2026 thread on ticket #162653 — Mikaela had
mentioned the trade-in question on the F14 (SN 20120002), and I wanted to
get you a concrete number before that conversation goes cold.

The F14 is a 2012-era predicate of the modern VasoGuard line. It still
runs, but it's been off active development for years and replacement parts
get harder every quarter. Two practical paths from here:

1. *Stay on the F14*  -- we'll keep supporting it as long as parts are
   available, no change.

2. *Trade in to a V-series*  -- we credit $10,000 toward any V-series
   regardless of age or condition (good through 06/2026). For HSHS Breese
   the most likely fit is the V8: full vascular lab, calibrated PVR,
   integrated hardware (no PC dependency), 5+5 year warranty.

    V8 list:        $32,900
    Trade-in:      -$10,000
    Net to you:    $22,900

At a conservative 8 ABI / segmental studies per week, CPT 93923
reimbursement (~$137.47) puts the payback inside 5 months -- and the V8
unlocks segmental and Calibrated PVR studies the F14 can't run today.

Happy to put a formal quote in front of you this week, or jump on a 15-min
call if you want to walk through the swap-out logistics. What's easier on
your end?

Thanks,
Spencer

